msgstr ""
":ref:`TECS_SINK_MAX "
"<TECS_SINK_MAX>`：设置控制器将使用的最大下降率（米/秒）。如果此值过大，飞机在下降时可能会超速。应设置为不超过最低俯仰角限制且不使飞机超速的可达值。"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:456
#: 95f1d1c069894c0186ec7e5eee5e07fb
msgid "Algorithm Overview"
msgstr "算法概述"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:458
#: 14e7a754c3d648059aa06607fc6edb83
msgid ""
"TECS stands for Total Energy Control System and for Plane refers to a new "
"control algorithm that coordinates throttle and pitch angle demands to "
"control the aircraft's height and airspeed. The underlying physics behind "
"the operation of TECS is simple, but to understand how it works you need to "
"understand the two types of mechanical energy that TECS controls. These are:"
msgstr ""
"TECS代表总能量控制系统，对于Plane而言，是指一种协调油门和俯仰角需求以控制飞机高度和空速的新控制算法。TECS运行背后的物理原理很简单，但要理解其工作原理，您需要了解TECS控制的两种机械能类型，分别是："

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:469
#: d106ed5d17df498f99ddf026efd317e0
msgid "and,"
msgstr "以及，"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:475
#: 18952ee797a64482b168d9596d585194
msgid ""
"Gravitational Potential Energy is the energy stored in an object due to its "
"height and is proportional to the height of the object. We all know "
"intuitively that to raise the height of an object requires energy and that "
"when an object falls energy is released. Similarly, to increase the height "
"of our aircraft requires more energy, which means more throttle is required."
msgstr ""
"重力势能是物体因其高度而储存的能量，与物体高度成正比。我们直觉上都知道，提升物体高度需要能量，而物体下落时会释放能量。同样，增加飞机高度需要更多能量，这意味着需要更多油门。"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:482
#: 0ac282dd63f8496f9b8818877c2c3b4a
msgid ""
"Kinetic energy is the energy stored in an object due to its velocity and is "
"proportional to velocity squared. An example is a rifle bullet, which "
"although it doesn't weigh very much, has a lot of energy due to its high "
"speed. Our aircraft don't travel at the speeds of rifle bullet, but they do "
"require energy to be supplied to increase their speed."
msgstr ""
"动能是物体因其速度而储存的能量，与速度的平方成正比。一个例子是步枪子弹，虽然重量不大，但由于高速而具有大量能量。我们的飞机达不到步枪子弹的速度，但确实需要能量来提高速度。"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:488
#: 2b711150d7854c4a99487da0ee645f56
msgid ""
"The total energy of the aircraft is the sum of the gravitational potential "
"energy and the kinetic energy. The drag acting on an aircraft in flight is "
"continually reducing its total energy, so the only way to maintain height "
"and speed is to supply thrust using a motor or utilise energy from some "
"other external source such as a rising air current. TECS calculates the "
"total energy required based on the demanded speed and height and adjusts the"
" throttle to maintain total energy at the demanded value."
msgstr ""
"飞机的总能量是重力势能和动能的总和。飞行中作用于飞机的阻力持续减少其总能量，因此维持高度和速度的唯一方法是使用电机提供推力或利用来自上升气流等其他外部来源的能量。TECS根据需求速度和高度计算所需的总能量，并调整油门以将总能量维持在需求值。"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:497
#: 027df4fcef3f40e4a2b790e8b3fb0963
msgid ""
"The other job of the TECS algorithm is to ensure that the balance between "
"gravitational potential and kinetic energy is correct. For example if the "
"aircraft is flying too slow and too high simultaneously, its total energy "
"might be correct, but there is too much potential energy and not enough "
"kinetic energy. TECS tries to maintain the correct balance between potential"
" and kinetic energy by adjusting the demanded pitch angle. By lowering the "
"nose energy is transferred from gravitational potential to kinetic energy or"
" vice-versa."
msgstr ""
"TECS算法的另一个任务是确保重力势能和动能之间的平衡正确。例如，如果飞机同时飞得太慢且太高，其总能量可能正确，但势能过多而动能不足。TECS通过调整需求俯仰角来尝试维持势能和动能之间的正确平衡。通过低头，能量从重力势能转移到动能，反之亦然。"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:506
#: 27ae4ef306e84d8bb454d7708ed9e1e1
msgid ""
"How much weighting is placed on kinetic energy or speed errors vs potential "
"energy or height errors is controlled by the "
":ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` parameter. At the default setting of "
"1.0, even weight is placed on speed and height errors. If  "
":ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` is set to 0.0 then the pitch angle "
"demand will respond 100% to height errors and ignore speed and if set to 2.0"
" will respond 100% to speed errors and ignore height."
msgstr ""
"动能或速度误差与势能或高度误差的权重由 :ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` "
"参数控制。在默认设置1.0时，速度和高度误差被赋予相等的权重。如果 :ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` "
"设置为0.0，则俯仰角需求将100%响应高度误差并忽略速度；如果设置为2.0，则将100%响应速度误差并忽略高度。"

#: ../../source/docs/tecs-total-energy-control-system-for-speed-height-tuning-guide.rst:514
#: 3a75d2e3a26644b78314eea3f588554e
msgid ""
"If the airspeed measurement is not used (as selected by setting "
":ref:`ARSPD_USE<ARSPD_USE>` and :ref:`ARSPD2_USE<ARSPD2_USE>`  = 0), then "
"the pitch angle will be used 100% to control height and the throttle will be"
" calculated from the demanded pitch angle."
msgstr ""
"如果不使用空速测量（通过设置 :ref:`ARSPD_USE<ARSPD_USE>` 和 :ref:`ARSPD2_USE<ARSPD2_USE>` ="
" 0选择），则俯仰角将100%用于控制高度，油门将根据需求俯仰角计算。"
